WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.824 --> 00:00:15.432
My stood in the doorway, frowning at me.

2
00:00:15.452 --> 00:00:18.794
"We're making healthy candy," I explained.

3
00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:24.477
"What you're making," said Mom, "is a big mess!"

4
00:00:25.838 --> 00:00:26.879
I looked around my room.

5
00:00:27.959 --> 00:00:29.100
It was sort of a mess.

6
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.517
Okay, it was a huge mess.

7
00:00:34.118 --> 00:00:36.239
"I want you to clean up," she said.

8
00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:38.219
"Right now, please!"

9
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.882
After Mom left, I nibbled on a chocolate-covered lima bean.

10
00:00:44.822 --> 00:00:46.042
It tasted awful.

11
00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:52.365
"Maybe my invention wasn't such a great idea after all," I said to Molly.

12
00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:57.527
Just then my friends Josh and Jenny knocked on my bedroom door.

13
00:00:57.547 --> 00:01:00.593
"Iggy, Molly," Josh said.

14
00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:02.894
"I have something to tell—Whoa!

15
00:01:03.254 --> 00:01:05.055
What a mess!"

16
00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:08.557
"We were making healthy candy," I explained.

17
00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:10.919
"But it didn't turn out so great."

18
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.161
Tate heard us talking and looked in too.

19
00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:16.602
"Wow!" he said.

20
00:01:16.622 --> 00:01:19.264
"It looks like a tornado blew through here!"

21
00:01:21.025 --> 00:01:25.408
I decided to clean up the mess fast, so everyone would quit talking about it.

22
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:30.982
By this time the frozen vegetables were thawing, and the chocolate syrup was melting.

23
00:01:32.222 --> 00:01:35.244
My friends helped me throw the soggy mess into the trash.

24
00:01:39.045 --> 00:01:40.546
well," I sighed.

25
00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.507
"My brilliant invention was a flop."

26
00:01:44.768 --> 00:01:46.869
"I have an idea," said Molly.

27
00:01:46.889 --> 00:01:50.510
"My aunt Grace sent me some money for my birthday.

28
00:01:51.631 --> 00:01:54.972
Why don't we all go to the Strawberry Store and get a treat?"

29
00:01:56.288 --> 00:01:57.648
"Great!" I said.

30
00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.149
I love the Strawberry Store.

31
00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:07.971
It sells things with strawberries like strawberry cupcakes, strawberry bubble gum, and strawberry ice cream.

32
00:02:09.272 --> 00:02:13.193
We all got permission to go except for Caswell who had a soccer game.

33
00:02:14.353 --> 00:02:16.894
Josh decided to bring his dog, Bunch, too.

34
00:02:18.134 --> 00:02:21.215
On the way to the store, Josh finished telling us his news.

35
00:02:21.235 --> 00:02:25.596
"Our dad lost his job at the Green Apple Supermarket."

36
00:02:26.432 --> 00:02:30.194
"Today is his last day," added Jenny sadly.

37
00:02:30.214 --> 00:02:33.756
"Then he has to look for a new job."

38
00:02:33.776 --> 00:02:39.599
"If he doesn't find one soon, we'll have to live with my grandmother," said Josh.

39
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.621
"She lives far away, in Ohio."

40
00:02:42.641 --> 00:02:46.263
"But you can't move!"

41
00:02:46.843 --> 00:02:47.584
said Molly.

42
00:02:47.604 --> 00:02:50.585
"That would be terrible," I agreed.

43
00:02:51.766 --> 00:02:55.168
Jenny and Josh had lived in our apartment building for a long time.

44
00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.421
Josh looked worried.

45
00:02:57.441 --> 00:03:01.743
"Iggy, can you invent something to help my dad find a job?"

46
00:03:01.763 --> 00:03:04.264
"I don't know," I said.

47
00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:07.425
"I'd have to be a real genius to do that."

48
00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:13.288
I looked at my friends, hoping that one of them would say that I was a real genius.

49
00:03:14.288 --> 00:03:19.971
After all, I'd invented some great things, like my incredible magic thinking box.

50
00:03:21.091 --> 00:03:22.792
No one said I was a genius though.

51
00:03:24.072 --> 00:03:27.894
Instead Molly stopped in front of the window of the Strawberry Store.

52
00:03:27.914 --> 00:03:33.256
"Look," she said, pointing to a sign: "Strawberry Sweepstakes!

53
00:03:33.576 --> 00:03:36.478
Buy Raffle Tickets for a Mountain Getaway For Six!"

54
00:03:36.498 --> 00:03:39.879
"What's a mountain getaway?"

55
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.020
asked Jenny.

56
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.342
"It's when you go away—to the mountains," I said.

57
00:03:45.362 --> 00:03:47.883
"Oh." Jenny nodded.

58
00:03:47.903 --> 00:03:49.564
"That sounds like fun."

59
00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.481
Inside Molly bought strawberry treats for everyone.

60
00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:58.262
Josh and Jenny got strawberry ice cream.

61
00:03:59.022 --> 00:04:00.303
Molly and I got cupcakes.

62
00:04:01.263 --> 00:04:04.384
Molly also bought a strawberry lollipop for Caswell.

63
00:04:05.624 --> 00:04:08.845
She said it was going to taste much better than the healthy candy.

64
00:04:10.226 --> 00:04:13.047
Then she decided to buy us each a raffle ticket too.

65
00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:17.568
"Ruff!" barked Bunch as Rose gave us the tickets.

66
00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:22.147
She laughed and then handed another ticket to Josh.

67
00:04:25.329 --> 00:04:27.051
"Here's one for your dog too."

68
00:04:29.913 --> 00:04:31.855
We wrote our names on the raffle tickets.

69
00:04:33.096 --> 00:04:34.457
Josh wrote Bunch's name.

70
00:04:35.818 --> 00:04:37.379
Then we gave them back to Rose.

71
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:43.604
That night I slept in my new bedroom for the first time.

72
00:04:44.656 --> 00:04:48.982
I lay in bed, dreaming of all the wonderful things I could invent.

73
00:04:49.963 --> 00:04:50.544
Who knew?

74
00:04:51.445 --> 00:04:54.368
Maybe one of my ideas would even help Mr.

75
00:04:54.449 --> 00:04:56.051
Chen get a new job!
